timingator is a trimmed, standalone copy of the timing part of Mapperatorinator.

Mapperatorinator
  https://github.com/OliBomby/Mapperatorinator, commit 0e2b0e387aab4b35c64b0b11b12d47578dea7587
  Copyright (c) 2024 OliBomby, MIT License (the LICENSE file in this repository).
  Every file under src/timingator/ except timing_point.py, api.py's TimingModel, cli.py and the
  package __init__/__main__ modules is copied or adapted from it; each says at its top which
  upstream file it comes from and what changed. The Rust crate under rust/ is a port of the same
  code; each module says at its top which upstream files it ports.

Model weights
  The checkpoints (default OliBomby/Mapperatorinator-v32 on Hugging Face) are downloaded at run
  time and are not part of this repository. They are published by OliBomby under their own terms.

VarWhisper backbone
  src/timingator/model/varwhisper/ builds on the Whisper implementation in Hugging Face
  Transformers (https://github.com/huggingface/transformers), Apache License 2.0.

slider
  timing_point.py mirrors the constructor of slider's TimingPoint
  (https://github.com/llllllllll/slider, LGPL-3.0) so the adapted code can call it unchanged; no
  slider code is copied.

SciPy
  rust/src/signal.rs ports scipy.ndimage.gaussian_filter1d and scipy.signal.find_peaks
  (https://github.com/scipy/scipy), Copyright (c) 2001-2002 Enthought, Inc. and 2003-2024 SciPy
  Developers, BSD 3-Clause License.

ggml
  rust/src/gguf.rs and quant/ggml.py follow the GGUF format and the block formats of ggml
  (https://github.com/ggml-org/ggml, as used in llama.cpp), Copyright (c) 2023-2024 The ggml
  authors, MIT License. quant/calib.py implements GPTQ (Frantar et al., 2022,
  arXiv:2210.17323).
